    "title": "2026 NBA Rookie of the Year Odds: Flagg Extends Lead Against Knueppel",
    "text": "Want to get more Covers content? Add us as a preferred source on your Google account here.It's amazing what a single weekend can do for your NBA Rookie of the Year candidacy.Dallas Mavericks forward Cooper Flagg reclaimed the lead in one of the most tightly contested races in recent memory by scoring 96 points over two games: A 51-point performance against Orlando and a 45-point, eight-rebound, nine-assist outing vs. the Lakers.AdvertisementThose two games were enough to move Flagg's flagging odds from +230 to -200, allowing him to leapfrog former Duke teammate Kon Knueppel — and Flagg has extended his lead on the NBA Rookie of the Year odds board by following that outburst with a 25/9 effort, then recording his first career triple-double.With Knueppel also slowing down (13 or fewer points in five of his last seven games), let's take a closer look at the latest NBA ROY odds as we approach the final weekend of regular-season action.PlayerOddsImplied probabilityCooper Flagg-26066.7%Kon Knueppel+19541.7%No. 1-overall pick Cooper Flagg was the clear odds-on favorite most of the season, sitting as short as -700 (an implied probability of 87.5%) over a month ago. However, Charlotte's Knueppel surpassed him in early March, and it's been a roller-coaster ever since:DateOddsMarch 27Knueppel: -210Flagg: +165March 28Knueppel: -255Flagg: +195March 29Knueppel: -240Flagg: +185March 30Knueppel: -250Flagg: +190March 31Knueppel: -260Flagg: +200April 1Knueppel: -250Flagg: +190April 3*Flagg scores 51Knueppel: -300Flagg: +225April 4Knueppel: -250Flagg: +185April 5*Flagg scores 45Knueppel: -330Flagg: +230April 6Knueppel: +140Flagg: -200Flagg vs Knueppel by the numbersPlayerPTSREBASTFlagg21.06.74.6Knueppel18.75.33.4Cash your ML bets quicker with bet365's early win payout!Take advantage of the early win payout at bet365, where any pre-game NBA moneyline bet gets paid out as a winner if your team goes up by 20+ points!AdvertisementLearn more about this feature, and all of bet3